  "id": "eastern_bluebird",
  "name": "Eastern bluebird",
  "description": "Temperate islands, wherever there is water with trees about: a small thrush, bright blue above and rust on the breast. A land bird among the waterbirds: it never comes down on water or boats, and keeps to treetops, stumps and boulders with short drops to the bank. Low, quick flight in bursts of wingbeats; pairs and small family parties; a soft warble (\"chur-lee, chur-wi\"). Drawn half as big again as life, to be seen at all on a phone.",
